        <mxCell id="dit-112" value="&lt;b&gt;The Diffusion Transformer (DiT) architecture.&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;Left:&lt;/i&gt; We train conditional latent DiT models. The input latent is decomposed into patches and processed by several DiT blocks. &lt;i&gt;Right:&lt;/i&gt; Details of our DiT blocks. We experiment with variants of standard transformer blocks that incorporate conditioning via adaptive layer norm, cross-attention and extra input tokens. Adaptive layer norm works best." style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=19.6;fontColor=#000000;" vertex="1" parent="dit-figure">
          <mxGeometry x="0" y="552" width="1314" height="78.6" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
